 "summary": "The global forward/backward flow, the set-level gluing (`union_of_isClosed`) and time-reversal (`comp_neg`) lemmas, and the arrival-at-boundary lemma have no counterpart in Mathlib (whose uniform-time existence requires `BoundarylessManifold`) or TauCeti (whose `BoundaryFlow/*` only flows near `\u2202M \u00d7 {0}`). The PR reuses `HasMFDerivWithinAt.union`, `IsMIntegralCurveOn.comp_mul`/`comp_add`, `not_isOutwardPointing_curveVelocityWithin_Ici` and `injOn_flowOut_boundary`, and derives the existing `IsMIntegralCurve.comp_neg` from the new set version.",
